  "@type": "Capability",
  "critical": false,
  "description": "Systematic methods for detecting and locating leaks in vacuum systems: helium mass spectrometer leak detection (vacuum mode and sniffer mode, sensitivity to 10⁻¹² atm·cc/s), pressure rise testing for overall integrity assessment, residual gas analysis (RGA) for leak-vs-outgassing discrimination, bubble testing for gross leaks, ultrasonic leak detection, and vacuum brazing/welding techniques for achieving hermetic seals. Distinct from vacuum measurement (pressure quantification) — leak detection identifies and localizes the pathways through which gas enters a vacuum system.",
  "early_win": false,
